WEBVTT

00:00.020 --> 00:02.480
<b>Tower, 1st Floor: The Gate of Pruning</b>

00:02.690 --> 00:05.230
<b>Tower, 1st Floor: The Pruning Ceremonial Hall</b>

00:03.130 --> 00:08.490
Other than that ice guy, 
I don't see any promising mages.

00:05.280 --> 00:08.490
<b>Head of the Wind Faction
Irvin Aurus</b>

00:08.890 --> 00:15.240
No... For better or worse,
there's one more attracting attention.

00:09.240 --> 00:12.990
<b>Ice Faction Aide-de-Camp
Sarissa Alfeld</b>

00:20.420 --> 00:22.880
<b>Will Serfort</b>

00:21.120 --> 00:24.380
You're just dodging! 
What are you doing, laggard?!

00:22.460 --> 00:24.380
<b>Julius Reinberg</b>

00:24.380 --> 00:26.510
He's wrong. That's...

00:24.500 --> 00:26.510
<b>Lightning Faction
Lihanna Owenzaus</b>

00:26.630 --> 00:28.510
<b>Earth Faction
Colette Loire</b>

00:26.900 --> 00:28.510
He's watching.

00:29.020 --> 00:31.220
Kiki, let me do this on my own.

00:32.830 --> 00:37.100
<i>That sad expression earlier... 
This is what it was about, right, Elfie?</i>

00:37.630 --> 00:40.100
<i>You were saying, 
"I'm sorry I couldn't scout you."</i>

00:38.100 --> 00:40.100
<b>Magia Vander Albis Vina
Five Supreme Wands, Icemaiden's Wand
Elfaria Albis Serfort</b>

00:41.180 --> 00:42.860
<i>But it's all right.</i>

00:43.370 --> 00:47.110
<i>I'll make it to where you are 
on my own two legs!</i>

00:59.880 --> 01:00.830
He's fast!

01:00.830 --> 01:02.610
No, more than that...

01:00.960 --> 01:03.460
<b>Elf Faction Aide-de-Camp
Filvis Challia</b>

01:00.960 --> 01:03.460
<b>Elf Faction Aide-de-Camp
Lefiya Viridis</b>

01:02.610 --> 01:03.460
He's strong.

01:03.780 --> 01:06.960
Splitting a Zoctonia in two 
from above its shields...

01:04.090 --> 01:06.960
<b>Fire Faction Aide-de-Camp
Logwell</b>

01:07.050 --> 01:10.880
<b>Lightning Faction Aide-de-Camp
Guilford Zurgas</b>

01:07.240 --> 01:10.290
He's even seen through every one 
of his opponent's moves.

01:10.290 --> 01:12.010
And in so short a time?

01:12.410 --> 01:14.720
<i>I've already seen that attack!</i>

01:15.840 --> 01:18.270
<i>I can see my opponent's moves 
more clearly than before!</i>

01:18.720 --> 01:21.000
<i>This Gloria is so flexible and light!</i>

01:21.000 --> 01:22.980
<i>It's so easy to move around in!</i>

01:22.980 --> 01:25.480
<i>This blade Mister Donnan forged
can cut through everything!</i>

01:25.780 --> 01:29.010
<i>Right now, I feel like I can do anything!</i>

01:33.860 --> 01:35.740
There's still more coming?!

01:37.870 --> 01:39.580
Glace Itier!

01:40.990 --> 01:41.910
Not good!

01:41.910 --> 01:42.790
A stray shot is—

01:43.540 --> 01:45.560
Julius, sorry! I'm gonna borrow this!

01:54.550 --> 01:56.680
Fully Charged...

01:57.640 --> 01:59.180
Glauss Wis!

01:59.560 --> 02:00.710
Will!

02:02.480 --> 02:03.710
Load!

02:03.710 --> 02:04.790
Burst!

02:08.950 --> 02:10.570
Glauss Mill!

02:15.820 --> 02:17.410
What just happened?

02:17.410 --> 02:21.830
Blizzard and sword-wind magic? 
Wait, was it really magic, though?

02:22.260 --> 02:25.510
Is that the Wis we saw at Terminalia?

02:26.580 --> 02:28.540
Oh, dear.

02:27.000 --> 02:30.170
<b>Clairie Serah</b>

02:28.540 --> 02:31.310
He went and beat all the Zoctonia.

02:31.310 --> 02:32.590
What're we gonna do about this?

02:50.550 --> 02:52.740
A blessing from Albis Vina.

02:53.180 --> 02:54.910
He's been scouted by the ice faction.

02:55.750 --> 02:57.240
And that's not all!

02:57.240 --> 03:00.740
Incindia Barham, too! 
That's the fire faction!

02:58.990 --> 03:00.740
<b>Magia Vander Incindia Barham
Five Supreme Wands, Flame Emperor's Wand
Cariot Incindia Wiseman</b>

03:00.740 --> 03:01.990
<b>Elf Faction
Wignall Lindor</b>

03:01.180 --> 03:01.990
Plus also...

03:01.990 --> 03:03.000
<b>Earth Faction Aide-de-Camp
 Frune Owdatid</b>

03:01.990 --> 03:03.000
<b>Head of the Earth Faction
Worguns Prehnite</b>

03:01.990 --> 03:03.000
<b>Earth Faction Aide-de-Camp 
Hammon Fossilis</b>

03:02.430 --> 03:04.000
the earth, wind...

03:04.330 --> 03:06.250
<b>Dark Faction</b>

03:04.550 --> 03:06.250
and even the dark factions!

03:06.370 --> 03:09.210
<b>Director of the Upper Institute 
& Head of the Colorless Faction
Kreutz Harlon</b>

03:06.650 --> 03:09.860
He's not a Multos
 with multiple affinities,

03:09.860 --> 03:13.280
yet five different factions 
have given him their blessing!

03:09.880 --> 03:13.090
<b>Aide to the Director of the Upper Institute 
Charles Lauer</b>

03:13.630 --> 03:17.010
I can't believe it. 
This is unprecedented, isn't it?

03:17.130 --> 03:19.390
<b>Fire Faction
Sion Ulster</b>

03:19.390 --> 03:21.640
He went and stole the credit.

03:23.890 --> 03:25.640
<b>Magia Vander Thorzeus Fasce
Five Supreme Wands, Lightning Lord's Wand
Zeo Thorzeus Reinbolt</b>

03:25.990 --> 03:28.340
In the event that multiple 
blessings are bestowed,

03:28.340 --> 03:31.220
the individual gains the right to choose.

03:32.140 --> 03:35.650
Which faction do you wish 
to join, Will Serfort?

03:43.430 --> 03:44.540
I...

03:44.540 --> 03:45.730
Wait.

03:50.130 --> 03:53.800
His "magic" isn't the sort of thing 
we ought to call magic.

04:15.030 --> 04:19.740
Episode 19
He Said He Would No Longer Hang His Head

05:30.860 --> 05:34.220
Your contributions during the Terminalia
incident were taken into account,

05:34.220 --> 05:36.780
and you were allowed to ascend
to the tower in their honor.

05:36.780 --> 05:38.230
That is all well and good.

05:38.500 --> 05:43.110
Yet are you truly qualified to be accepted
into one of our glorious factions?

05:43.110 --> 05:45.340
I cannot help but wonder.

05:46.270 --> 05:48.930
Were you not watching, Kreutz?

05:49.410 --> 05:51.870
Just now, he used a magic spell.

05:52.180 --> 05:54.760
I was indeed watching, Lady Elfaria.

05:55.360 --> 05:57.500
However, while you might say 
he used magic,

05:57.500 --> 06:00.130
he merely repurposed someone else's spell.

06:00.680 --> 06:03.740
His true nature is, after all, 
not that of a mage,

06:03.740 --> 06:06.010
but of an extremely violent warrior.

06:06.670 --> 06:10.300
We would be welcoming one no better 
than a dwarf into the tower.

06:10.300 --> 06:13.140
What condemnation 
would the world level at us?

06:13.960 --> 06:16.650
The mere thought is terrifying.

06:17.030 --> 06:19.900
Get to the point. 
What are you trying to say?

06:17.480 --> 06:19.900
<b>Magia Vander Elleaf Canaan
Five Supreme Wands, Sacred Elf's Wand
Ellenor Ljos Alf</b>

06:20.340 --> 06:23.260
This, plain and simple, Lady Ellenor.

06:23.260 --> 06:26.410
If he has even a hint 
of aptitude as a wand,

06:26.410 --> 06:28.720
then he must prove it to us.

06:41.710 --> 06:45.740
We developed these magical creatures 
for the purpose of suppressing dwarves.

06:45.740 --> 06:47.470
They are Wors Oozes.

06:47.470 --> 06:49.180
Observe.

06:49.180 --> 06:50.460
Crysto Wreath.

06:54.130 --> 06:55.220
As you can see,

06:55.220 --> 06:58.940
contact with magical energy from even
low-level spells makes them disintegrate.

06:58.940 --> 07:02.440
Put another way, these creatures, 
which are made of viscous liquid,

07:02.440 --> 07:06.200
cannot be felled by anyone
incapable of producing magical energy.

07:13.830 --> 07:15.830
<i>My sword has no effect!</i>

07:16.220 --> 07:18.080
<i>It's just like that time with the Balkar!</i>

07:19.000 --> 07:22.500
<i>Do these nullify any and all 
physical attacks?</i>

07:28.260 --> 07:30.890
What are you gonna do about this?

07:31.370 --> 07:34.000
There is sense to what Kreutz says.

07:34.480 --> 07:36.940
Let's have him demonstrate
one such battle.

07:37.750 --> 07:41.390
As a Magia Vander, I must say this...

07:41.390 --> 07:44.030
The tower is the apex 
of the magical world.

07:44.030 --> 07:49.170
A sword who cannot use magic of his own 
will not be permitted to advance here.

07:51.620 --> 07:54.370
<i>No matter how much I cut them, 
it does no good!</i>

07:54.370 --> 07:58.500
<i>But creatures like this always have cores!</i>

07:58.500 --> 08:00.170
<i>If I can just crush that...</i>

08:04.090 --> 08:05.590
How shortsighted.

08:07.800 --> 08:10.090
If their bodies could be made liquid,

08:10.090 --> 08:13.780
why did you think the same
 would not be true of their cores?

08:14.220 --> 08:17.730
Do not underestimate us. 
This is magic perfected.

08:17.730 --> 08:19.230
This is the tower!

08:20.850 --> 08:22.180
<i>An electric discharge?</i>

08:27.860 --> 08:31.290
A stunning shock capable
 of stopping a dwarf...

08:31.290 --> 08:34.870
The stuff you make
 is always so nasty, Kreutz.

08:38.580 --> 08:39.620
Hey...

08:39.750 --> 08:43.290
<b>Lyril Mars</b>

08:39.750 --> 08:43.290
<b>Gordon Valley</b>

08:39.900 --> 08:41.160
This is bad, isn't it?

08:41.600 --> 08:43.630
At this rate, he'll...

08:52.770 --> 08:56.140
We're high mages now, too!

08:56.560 --> 09:00.140
If our magic will let him 
use that Wis thing, then...

09:04.430 --> 09:06.430
Do not do anything uncalled for.

09:06.780 --> 09:10.530
This is not an audition 
for the two of you.

09:10.530 --> 09:14.470
The aim is to excise alien elements. 
This is an inquisitional hearing.

09:30.790 --> 09:32.760
<i>I know you're more than this!</i>

09:32.760 --> 09:34.190
<i>Aren't you?!</i>

09:53.220 --> 09:54.280
<i>Not yet...</i>

09:55.670 --> 09:58.540
I'm not giving up yet!

10:04.950 --> 10:07.960
Any more of this would simply
be a waste of time.

10:07.960 --> 10:10.800
As I thought, he is not qualified.

10:13.300 --> 10:15.390
I believe he should remain colorless

10:15.390 --> 10:20.280
and have his name entered in 
the lowest ranks of our Upper Institute.

10:20.280 --> 10:23.270
The Wis power that defeated 
the Devander was,

10:23.270 --> 10:25.970
without exaggeration, truly tremendous.

10:27.310 --> 10:29.780
I will reveal the unknown within him

10:29.780 --> 10:34.820
and ensure that such power 
serves the magical world well.

10:35.300 --> 10:37.950
So he will be a lab animal, then?

10:38.380 --> 10:42.850
If it means we may understand 
the fifth element and make use of it,

10:42.850 --> 10:47.550
then I see no problem with any of 
our organizations taking charge of him.

10:47.550 --> 10:48.340
However...

10:54.720 --> 10:59.720
This isn't something to throw a temper 
tantrum over like a child, Elfaria.

10:59.720 --> 11:02.960
Kreutz, this isn't what we discussed.

11:03.350 --> 11:07.230
Right now, I am very close to snapping!

11:09.380 --> 11:11.230
E-Elfie?

11:11.500 --> 11:14.610
All this squawking is annoying, 
you degenerates!

11:19.740 --> 11:22.620
We'll be holding another Bloom anyway.

11:22.620 --> 11:25.500
You can leave all your 
tedious talk until then, can't you?

11:25.500 --> 11:26.330
What?

11:26.750 --> 11:30.910
If this were any normal year, the next 
Bloom would be in six months' time.

11:31.590 --> 11:34.490
However, after the losses 
we suffered at Terminalia,

11:34.490 --> 11:38.760
restoring the lost manpower of each 
faction has become urgent business.

11:39.180 --> 11:41.580
Hence, this year will be an exception,

11:41.580 --> 11:45.160
and the Second Bloom 
is scheduled for a week from now.

11:45.770 --> 11:47.850
After overcoming such a tragedy,

11:47.850 --> 11:51.690
you have more room for growth 
than anyone else in the magical world,

11:51.690 --> 11:53.430
Grim Generation.

11:53.430 --> 11:55.150
The tower... No.

11:55.690 --> 11:58.660
The world has high hopes for you!

11:58.980 --> 12:03.050
In fact, if you're not working hard enough
that you vomit blood, we'll have problems.

12:03.050 --> 12:06.860
So to those of you who did not 
receive blessings today,

12:06.860 --> 12:09.290
stir yourselves to do better
 at the next Bloom.

12:09.630 --> 12:12.280
Will Serfort, that includes you.

12:13.860 --> 12:19.150
That works for everyone, Upper Institute 
and noble Magia Vander alike, no?

12:19.590 --> 12:21.960
There is but one rule in the tower...

12:21.960 --> 12:24.060
"Prove your worth," right?

12:25.810 --> 12:27.230
Very well.

12:27.230 --> 12:29.100
After all, we ourselves

12:29.100 --> 12:33.320
continued to prove our worth, 
which is how we came to be Magia Vander.

12:44.950 --> 12:47.200
So this little farce ends here.

13:05.470 --> 13:06.720
Everyone...

13:13.100 --> 13:14.110
Will...

13:17.980 --> 13:21.720
What a waste of time. 
I can't even bring myself to sigh.

13:31.670 --> 13:34.210
In a week, we'll have 
to face this test again?

13:36.270 --> 13:37.090
Hey!

13:44.810 --> 13:46.170
Are you crying?

13:46.600 --> 13:49.600
No, it's just too funny.

13:51.470 --> 13:52.730
Funny?

13:53.100 --> 13:54.180
Yeah.

13:57.110 --> 13:59.360
Things like adversity 
and tough situations...

14:00.110 --> 14:03.360
As soon as I feel like something's 
within reach, I always get knocked down.

14:13.870 --> 14:16.130
All right!

14:16.130 --> 14:20.010
No matter how many tries it takes, 
I swear I'll overcome this!

14:28.240 --> 14:29.450
That was unexpected.

14:30.310 --> 14:32.020
What was, Gil?

14:32.300 --> 14:37.270
That you, Lord Zeo, didn't bestow your
blessing on Will Serfort after all that.

14:38.950 --> 14:41.570
I thought you liked people like him.

14:45.360 --> 14:47.120
Moron.

14:47.120 --> 14:49.700
You still don't understand me?

14:56.210 --> 15:00.710
The guys that drag themselves up 
from rock bottom are more entertaining...

15:01.170 --> 15:03.370
Not to mention stronger, y'know?

15:05.630 --> 15:08.970
<b><u>Wist-Set Silver</u>

Master Donnan, you're amazing! To think you'd hammer such an incredible weapon!
But the mages keep really strict control of Wist gems, so they're rare materials, right? 
I'm amazed you were able to make this. Why are you looking away like that, Master?
D-Don't tell me you stole— Ow!

-An apprentice dwarven smith who got hit</b>

15:09.180 --> 15:10.470
<b>Fieldwind Wand</b>

15:10.560 --> 15:13.980
<b><u>Emma Klever</u>

Race: Rhizanth   Age: 16   Height: 165 cm
Birthday: 19th of Hallasmoon
Likes: Family, flurry kittens (lighsnows)
Dislikes: Flowers
Wants to Save: Ian Klever

Deepest Dungeon Floor Reached: 8th
Equipment: Fieldwind wand
Skills: Intermediate wind magic</b>

15:10.560 --> 15:13.980
<b>Part of the 41st graduating class, also known as the Grim Generation. 
She excels at writing and spellwork, but is no good at praxis, which some may call "the real deal."
 In actual combat, she tends to be among the least effective, even among her peers.
 If only she didn't lose her nerve, she'd have extremely high potential.
She has a brother named Ian, who is five years younger.
 All of her efforts are devoted to saving him from a rarely-spoken-of flowerbed syndrome.</b>

15:14.520 --> 15:17.980
<b>Tower, 1st Floor: Temporary Quarters</b>

15:17.980 --> 15:24.610
Fire, wind, earth, lightning, 
water, darkness, light...

15:25.220 --> 15:27.900
Excluding elven magic, I must look

15:27.900 --> 15:30.260
to these seven elements 
to find a new approach.

15:30.620 --> 15:34.100
A no-talent like me, if I had to say, 
possesses no magical affinity.

15:34.100 --> 15:37.870
But even though I can't cast magic, that
 doesn't mean I can't use magical energy.

15:37.870 --> 15:41.820
My ability to wield the power 
known as Wis proves that.

15:41.820 --> 15:45.400
If I can analyze this phenomenon 
and harness its energy, then...

15:46.520 --> 15:51.210
He's been studying like that all night, 
since the Bloom ended yesterday.

15:51.210 --> 15:53.700
I knew it. There's something 
wrong with that guy.

15:53.700 --> 15:54.720
All right!

15:55.750 --> 16:00.740
Do you have a minute, book-learner—
Um, say, do you mind if I call you Will?

16:00.740 --> 16:01.650
What?

16:02.150 --> 16:04.740
Th-That's fine, but...

16:04.740 --> 16:08.660
You're the one who spoke to me 
after the Grand Magic Festival, um...

16:08.990 --> 16:10.750
Emma Klever.

16:09.240 --> 16:13.450
<b>Emma Klever</b>

16:10.750 --> 16:15.200
We're thinking of heading into 
the dungeon until the next Bloom.

16:15.200 --> 16:17.660
We even got permission 
from the Upper Institute.

16:17.660 --> 16:20.170
Do you mean to train?

16:20.170 --> 16:21.440
Yes.

16:21.440 --> 16:25.900
We're technically high mages now, 
so we can go deeper than the tenth floor.

16:25.900 --> 16:27.770
Defeating that floor keeper

16:27.770 --> 16:32.240
seems to be the only way for all of us 
to practice working together.

16:32.240 --> 16:36.310
We want to get into the fire faction 
so that we can follow after Sion!

16:36.610 --> 16:38.460
So, do you want to come with us?

16:38.460 --> 16:42.340
I know this won't undo everything 
we've put you through before now,

16:42.830 --> 16:45.190
but if you'd like to join us...

16:46.230 --> 16:47.190
Yes, of course!

16:47.820 --> 16:48.700
No!

16:50.310 --> 16:52.860
This laggard is training with <i>me!</i>

16:52.860 --> 16:54.550
What? What does that mean?

16:54.550 --> 16:55.800
Julius?

16:55.800 --> 16:59.710
Playing at being friends 
isn't what you need right now!

16:59.970 --> 17:02.710
It's getting control 
over that power called Wis!

17:03.330 --> 17:04.710
Control?

17:04.710 --> 17:07.460
And I will help you do just that!

17:08.770 --> 17:10.870
That would be a big help...

17:10.870 --> 17:12.470
but why go to the trouble?

17:13.460 --> 17:15.710
So much has transpired 
up to this point.

17:15.710 --> 17:17.720
But I, just like Wignall and the others...

17:23.180 --> 17:26.570
think of you as part of the team.

17:27.710 --> 17:30.110
P-Part of the team?

17:30.110 --> 17:31.910
Thank you, Julius!

17:31.910 --> 17:33.360
I'd love to have your help!

17:33.360 --> 17:37.050
I'm part of the team... part of the team!
I'm part of the team!

17:37.050 --> 17:38.420
<i>This is good.</i>

17:38.420 --> 17:41.780
<i>Who would really put themselves
 out for the no-talent?</i>

17:41.780 --> 17:45.380
<i>I'm only doing this 
for the sake of my future!</i>

17:45.650 --> 17:50.160
Thank you, Julius! It's all thanks to you!

17:46.230 --> 17:51.450
<i>I'll give Lady Elfaria's childhood friend 
a little push and earn points with her.</i>

17:51.450 --> 17:54.830
<i>This should certainly lead 
to redeeming myself in her eyes!</i>

17:51.450 --> 17:54.120
Well done. I've revised my opinion of you.

17:55.140 --> 17:58.200
<i>I'll use this pseudo-dwarf 
for all he's worth.</i>

17:58.200 --> 18:01.140
<i>I </i>will<i> get into the ice faction!</i>

18:01.550 --> 18:03.650
Stop dragging your heels, laggard!

18:04.030 --> 18:06.400
We're starting your training immediately!

18:11.140 --> 18:12.950
Yeah!

18:17.450 --> 18:20.250
<b>Tower, 1st Floor, East End: Fields of Solitude</b>

18:24.100 --> 18:25.920
<i>Fully Charged.</i>

18:27.250 --> 18:28.920
<i>Glauss Wis!</i>

18:29.600 --> 18:33.420
I tried charging it just like you said. 
What do I do now?

18:33.850 --> 18:36.300
Now you maintain it.

18:37.680 --> 18:41.530
Frozen whispers, 
quieten down and flutter a dance.

18:42.060 --> 18:46.060
Thy name is that of 
an ice bird guardian, Kotori.

18:48.780 --> 18:51.070
Fridde Gardinas!

18:52.570 --> 18:53.960
These are...

18:53.960 --> 18:55.910
They may be low-level guardians,

18:55.910 --> 18:58.040
but a good bit of magical energy 
went into them.

18:58.040 --> 18:59.990
It'll take more than
showering them with weak

18:59.990 --> 19:02.080
magic of the same element
 to get rid of them.

19:02.560 --> 19:05.790
Starting now, to keep from 
destroying these guardians,

19:05.790 --> 19:08.080
you will keep your energy
in check as you go about.

19:08.080 --> 19:09.840
What do you mean?

19:10.900 --> 19:13.270
You're going to take
 your Wis or whatever

19:13.270 --> 19:15.840
and learn how to activate it yourself.

19:17.090 --> 19:20.240
You attended the academy for six years,

19:20.240 --> 19:23.350
yet you couldn't even learn
the most rudimentary of magics.

19:23.350 --> 19:26.520
Even now, instead of trying 
to pick up a preexisting spell,

19:26.520 --> 19:30.860
it'd be far more constructive to harness
 the power you already possess!

19:31.260 --> 19:36.110
Maybe so, but how do I do that?

19:36.870 --> 19:40.970
I have to get my charge from others' magic
precisely <i>because</i> I can't use my own.

19:40.970 --> 19:43.390
I'm stuck relying on 
outside magical energy.

19:43.390 --> 19:47.900
For me to prepare magical energy to
 activate Wis on my own is contradictory.

19:47.900 --> 19:50.780
That's like trying to produce
 a one from a zero.

19:50.780 --> 19:53.320
It's no different than trying 
to create new magic, so—

19:52.280 --> 19:54.880
Oh, stop! Stop talking! 
Just stop all this theorizing!

19:55.210 --> 19:58.890
There's no point in settling on a harbor
you don't even know you can reach.

19:58.890 --> 20:02.230
What you're going to do now 
is extremely simple:

20:02.230 --> 20:04.270
anchor magical energy.

20:04.270 --> 20:05.710
Anchor it?

20:08.180 --> 20:10.600
Even if the magical energy 
happened to be mine,

20:10.600 --> 20:13.090
if you anchor it 
for the rest of your life,

20:13.090 --> 20:14.900
then it becomes yours, doesn't it?

20:16.170 --> 20:19.150
Let's say you currently output at 100,

20:19.150 --> 20:21.510
where a hundredth or thousandth
 of that would do.

20:21.510 --> 20:24.650
Just reduce the energy you output 
and continue to maintain it!

20:25.160 --> 20:27.340
Whether you're awake or asleep,

20:27.340 --> 20:29.940
you'll maintain that magical energy 
all your days.

20:29.940 --> 20:34.780
The ideal outcome is for you to control it
such that you only use it in battle.

20:34.780 --> 20:37.050
If you can do that, it's basically...

20:37.340 --> 20:38.410
as good as magic!

20:44.430 --> 20:48.690
At the next Bloom, you will 
undoubtedly face those oozes again.

20:49.020 --> 20:50.770
No matter how weak the magical energy,

20:50.770 --> 20:54.440
one touch of it and they fall apart. 
That was readily demonstrated.

20:54.440 --> 20:56.450
If all you need to do is 
defeat those things,

20:56.450 --> 20:59.700
then rationally speaking, it doesn't 
matter how little energy you have!

21:00.110 --> 21:03.530
There's a limit to what you can 
accomplish in less than a week!

21:03.530 --> 21:06.580
Work backward from your goal and 
minimize the challenges you tackle!

21:06.580 --> 21:09.580
You like to cram everything in, 
so you're terrible at outlining!

21:10.410 --> 21:14.160
<i>In order to keep from destroying 
the guardians in this practical exercise,</i>

21:14.160 --> 21:17.840
<i>I need a deft sense of anchoring 
magical energy in a long-lasting way.</i>

21:18.430 --> 21:22.090
<i>So these guardians are like restraints
to help me control my magical energy!</i>

21:22.650 --> 21:25.530
<i>How incredible! 
This all makes so much sense!</i>

21:25.530 --> 21:28.350
<i>He really wasn't in the Top Three 
at the academy for nothing!</i>

21:28.910 --> 21:31.100
Truly, thank you, Julius!

21:31.100 --> 21:35.120
You're so amazing! I wonder why 
none of the factions wanted you!

21:34.940 --> 21:36.480
STAB

21:36.480 --> 21:38.980
I-It's all your fault!

21:38.980 --> 21:43.070
Blast it!

21:43.070 --> 21:46.660
<b>Tower, 1st Floor: Colorless Garden</b>

21:53.110 --> 21:54.940
Ah, the springtime of youth.

21:55.500 --> 21:59.440
I do wonder how this special training 
of theirs will turn out.

23:28.050 --> 23:31.010
<b>Wistoria: Wand and Sword</b>

23:36.650 --> 23:39.230
Next time on <i>Wistoria: Wand and Sword</i>,

23:39.540 --> 23:42.620
episode 20, "Teachings of the Witch."

23:40.480 --> 23:45.990
Episode 20
Teachings of the Witch
